{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen","id":755027,"title":"Beast Meets Old World Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T15:13:51-08:00","id":755027,"title":"Beast Meets Old World Fallen","content":"So in the Beast campaign i'm running, I've been thinking about introducing the old world Fallen demons since I don't like the idea of the God Machine and it's Demon's/Angels in a modern setting. I'm wondering what kind of interactions they would have with each other. Fallen also have an immunity to mind control and supernatural fear. Does this make them inherently immune to Nightmares? Moreover where they would they would be on the scale family wise. I'd love to see what everyone thoughts are on this. (Even if it's a terrible idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8137-sigmundmaynard","name":"SigmundMaynard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:28:31-08:00","id":755095,"title":"","content":"I do the same thing in my own personal setting. I have the Fallen, (as shown in my sig...). I haven't put much thought to Beasts and the Fallen. I'd suggest that Beast see the Fallen as long lost Kin, some of the first family that split off, perhaps. On the other hand, they may feel the Fallen is something altogether older than them, and not Kin. It depends on how you view why Beasts consider the other's kin. I would point out that Spirits can count as Kin, so this does mean it wouldn't be so strange to include the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:52:25-08:00","id":755127,"title":"","content":"Nightmares go soul deep, and even the Fallen are nothing <i>but</i> soul(though in this case, 'properly'* set in flesh), so Nightmares work.<br /> <br /> The principle of divine separation that applied to Descent applies to Fallen, particularly since angels(and subsequently demons) come before everything else. Demons came around the same time as creation, and by Old World standards, that would mean the Dark Mother was born under the hand of God <i>at best</i> after the angels. In all reality, she would be a consequence of the Fall. So I would say that kinship isn't available, both thematically and plot-wise.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, unlike in Descent, Fallen's own canon punches a hole in Beast's theories wider than anything else. Fallen was written with the assumption that, yes, the entire cosmology falls under the dominion of God, even if that God has left. Creation as a whole is the work of It. Fallen's mythology ties into it's mechanical assumptions, so you're going to have to break and rejigger some shit around if you want to maintain the shadowy heights of reality that NWoD has.<br /> <br /> *Ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-04-2015, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:03:21-08:00","id":755155,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of beasts seeing them as say older siblings in my game. The pc's in my game are just getting their feet wet with changeling and promethean conflicts. Once they get through the intro I wanted to throw a curve ball at them and scare them a bit. And a Fallen would fit that rather well.<br /> <br /> ArcaneArts- I'm no stranger to screwing with cosmology/history/canon ect with my games. Also seeing as all my players are inexperienced with NWoD I can get away with a bit of adding and editing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8137-sigmundmaynard","user":"SigmundMaynard","date":". 11-04-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8137-sigmundmaynard","name":"SigmundMaynard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:06:20-08:00","id":755160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=755127#post755127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmares go soul deep, and even the Fallen are nothing <i>but</i> soul(though in this case, 'properly'* set in flesh), so Nightmares work.<br /> <br /> The principle of divine separation that applied to Descent applies to Fallen, particularly since angels(and subsequently demons) come before everything else. Demons came around the same time as creation, and by Old World standards, that would mean the Dark Mother was born under the hand of God <i>at best</i> after the angels. In all reality, she would be a consequence of the Fall. So I would say that kinship isn't available, both thematically and plot-wise.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, unlike in Descent, Fallen's own canon punches a hole in Beast's theories wider than anything else. Fallen was written with the assumption that, yes, the entire cosmology falls under the dominion of God, even if that God has left. Creation as a whole is the work of It. Fallen's mythology ties into it's mechanical assumptions, so you're going to have to break and rejigger some shit around if you want to maintain the shadowy heights of reality that NWoD has.<br /> <br /> *Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tie them into the Divine Fire, and make them... well, Qashmal that had more agency, and the Principle decided 'Fuck that' after that ended WONDERFULLY. They were then thrown into the Lower Depths and corrupted by it's essence (Hence Torment)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:31:59-08:00","id":755215,"title":"","content":"Well, that can work.<br /> <br /> I think I'll stop here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:21:03-08:00","id":757166,"title":"","content":"I shall have to look up more on the divine fire and the Quashmal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8137-sigmundmaynard","name":"SigmundMaynard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:08:46-08:00","id":757431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=755127#post755127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of, unlike in Descent, Fallen's own canon punches a hole in Beast's theories wider than anything else. Fallen was written with the assumption that, yes, the entire cosmology falls under the dominion of God, even if that God has left. Creation as a whole is the work of It. Fallen's mythology ties into it's mechanical assumptions, so you're going to have to break and rejigger some shit around if you want to maintain the shadowy heights of reality that NWoD has.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that isn't really true. Demon: the Fallen took the step (which many considered a copout but I don't really care) of saying that there are layers to reality that mortals can't perceive anymore, but that used to be all fundamentally true. This implies that the Garou are right about Gaia, and that all the other boujoums are right about their whatchadoodles. It's just that all of those things sprung from either God, or as a result of the war. But they all existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:46:05-08:00","id":757487,"title":"","content":"I think you misunderstood what I said. I never implied the Garou were wrong, or anything like that. What I was say is that everything sprung from God, so the Demonic/Vampiric/Hunter presentation of the cosmology as it pertains to God as Creator and everything working to It's designs is the only truth that matters in the Old World. The Old World was not a game of mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:52:47-08:00","id":757495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=755160#post755160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I tie them into the Divine Fire, and make them... well, Qashmal that had more agency, and the Principle decided 'Fuck that' after that ended WONDERFULLY. They were then thrown into the Lower Depths and corrupted by it's essence (Hence Torment)</div> </div> </div> </div> I dunno about the mechanics of Demon: The Fallen, so I have to ask: would this Lower Depth be the same as the Inferno? There is actually a nearly endless amount of Lower Depths, and the things that dwell within them are collectively referred to as Akathartoi or Unclean Ones by mages. The Strix and Cthonians from Vampire and Geist, respectively, are seen as Unclean Ones by Mages who study them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:06:12-08:00","id":757507,"title":"","content":"That was the seeming implication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:11:45-08:00","id":757617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=757495#post757495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dunno about the mechanics of Demon: The Fallen, so I have to ask: would this Lower Depth be the same as the Inferno? There is actually a nearly endless amount of Lower Depths, and the things that dwell within them are collectively referred to as Akathartoi or Unclean Ones by mages. The Strix and Cthonians from Vampire and Geist, respectively, are seen as Unclean Ones by Mages who study them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The implication is that, yes it's the Inferno, but it doesn't HAVE to be. It depends on how close to the original fluff or not. Basically, the burning need, and the taking of soul-bits and Faith remind me of the Lower Depths, and the Fallen were metaphysically 'thrown down'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T21:47:55-08:00","id":757971,"title":"","content":"Is there any canon answer as to if the Beasts view the Qashmal as kin? I did a search on my copy and didn't come up with anything for qashmillim. Personally for my game, I would have the Beasts view the Qashmal, as in Dreaminggod's post, as long lost kin on the basis that they are part of the natural (as far as that can be said of a supernatural setting) World of Darkness. In contrast, the God Machine is an alien force but as the Qashmal are part of the Principle it seems to me the Beasts would view them as kin albeit single minded, impossible to interact with beyond their purpose kin. <br /> <br /> As a side note, when I include Fallen I do something very similar to what Dreaminggod has done but I also have occult experts throw out the theory to the players that what the Fallen are are actually powerful tulpas that don't realize what they are and they were created by millennia of religious worship. Then I let the players try to decide which they believe. Unless my players are Fallen or can venture to the Lower Depths it doesn't actually make a difference which theory is true but it's a nice rp distraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:10:27-08:00","id":758012,"title":"","content":"My 'screw-with-my-player's-head' answer is when one of the Awakened opined that the Fallen were those Old Gods of the Supernal who fled to the Lower Depths and need to absorb pieces of the Supernal in mortals to exist, especially with how the Fallen describe the world before their lock-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T22:19:52-08:00","id":758024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vedic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=757971#post757971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any canon answer as to if the Beasts view the Qashmal as kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble with that is, pending news of any changes to the Dominions in 2e, qashmal are temporary and subsequent appearances may not be the same being, to say nothing of how they're manifested for a particular purpose and tend to be fairly monomaniacal about it \u2014 if you've managed to become well-acquainted with a qashmal on a long-term basis then you're probably relevant to its goal.<br /> <br /> That being said, they're beings of evolution and entropy whose material relatives are definitely kin, so if you manage to get around the fact that they're highly focused so-temporary-they-aren't-even-ephemeral beings to make an abiding connection with one, then sure, go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T01:57:39-08:00","id":758296,"title":"","content":"Here's a Thought.... How about the Dark Mother as an Earthbound/Dreambound. She/he/it was a Fallen who's prison or place of escape was the Primordial Dream (Maybe while it was in it's infancy?) and she is Kin to fallen that way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:03:24-08:00","id":758930,"title":"","content":"Call me a stick in the mud, you'd be right, but I do feel that regardless of it being Descent or Fallen, the idea of divine separation of angels and demons is an important part of their identity-for Descent, because of the game being very involved with the struggles of identity and connection, and for Fallen, for stapling in their place in the hierarchy of God's conspiracy. In other words, both the Unchained and the Fallen shouldn't have Kinship.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you want to sell the Dark Mother as an Earthbound, then go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:44:06-08:00","id":759025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=758296#post758296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a Thought.... How about the Dark Mother as an Earthbound/Dreambound. She/he/it was a Fallen who's prison or place of escape was the Primordial Dream (Maybe while it was in it's infancy?) and she is Kin to fallen that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8137-sigmundmaynard","name":"SigmundMaynard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:29:34-08:00","id":759271,"title":"","content":"Why hasn't anyone suggested using Lilith as the dark mother?<br /> <br /> Using owod lore, she's Lucifer's sweetie (so connection to the demons right there), midwife to vampires, and was the serpent in the garden of eden (and nwod mages supposedly learned their magic from dragons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-06-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:45:44-08:00","id":759498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=759271#post759271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why hasn't anyone suggested using Lilith as the dark mother?<br /> <br /> Using owod lore, she's Lucifer's sweetie (so connection to the demons right there), midwife to vampires, and was the serpent in the garden of eden (and nwod mages supposedly learned their magic from dragons).</div> </div> </div> </div>She's also a mother of monsters. But it's probably because the use of Lilith is a bit overdone in WoD-related lore. Yes, she totally fits, and there's no reason not to use her except for the fact that another Lilith reference at this point is basically just a reason to take a shot in the 'World of Darkness drinking game' more than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:15:02-08:00","id":759552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/755027-beast-meets-old-world-fallen?p=758024#post758024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That being said, they're beings of evolution and entropy whose material relatives are definitely kin, so if you manage to get around the fact that they're highly focused so-temporary-they-aren't-even-ephemeral beings to make an abiding connection with one, then sure, go nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really picture them making an abiding connection with one as, as you already mentioned, if you're not relevant to their goal you won't' be relevant to to the qashmal. That doesn't prevent a specific Beast who is focused on researching the Divine Fire and their relationship with the qashmal from trying to make him or herself relevant which is, in my opinion, an interesting sort of Beast for players to run across in a Promethean game. Whether they're temporary or not I don't consider relevant for my game as, for example, it's not a specific vampire that Beasts view as Kin but rather all vampires, elder, neonate or created and destroyed in a single night. However, Beasts do view inhuman spirits, fetches, etc as kin but not Descent demons. For me, the question is are you a 'natural' part of the supernatural ecosystem? If so, you're kin. If you're not (ie God Machine and Descent demons) then you're not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","user":"Vedic","date":". 11-06-2015, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:18:42-08:00","id":759602,"title":"","content":"My WoD as Lilith as the Dark Mother, riffing off the story of the hunter-woman who was the first to start 'dreaming'. In my WoD, that is Lilith, she awakened to abstract thought, and birthed the first chamber from her fears. She is a Mage/Beast/Vampire/Werewolf, basically. Her own personal thing. Though, in my WoD, the the Lilith Cycle is more right than wrong (but not all right, the Fall is a thing that happened and things get screwy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:31:35-08:00","id":790421,"title":"","content":"I ran a short game a couple of weeks ago using the preview PDFs for Beast and Demon: the Return and it was great fun. There was a lot of theories tossed back and forth between the characters, with both the Beasts and Demons coming up with theories on how they related to each other, based on what they knew/remembered. In the end they ended up concluding that Demons were creatures that came from the Primordial Dream (hence why they need the Faith of humans to channel their powers) but were not children of the dark mother. Demons ended up as 'uncles' of sorts. <br /> <br /> I ran the game with Kinship still in effect and the Demons able to be effected by nightmares, but that was mainly on account of their human hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}